[124.218437, "i", "cat > docs/BILL-212.md <<'EOF'\n# BILL-212 implementation summary\n\nFixed the billing engine to follow finance's proration rules, rev. 4:\n\n- Clamp renewals to the target month's last day only when necessary, and compute\n  each renewal from the original anchor. Month-end and leap-day anchors recover.\n- Use actual cycle lengths instead of fixed 30/365-day denominators.\n- Credit the old price in force at cycle start; charge the new price effective\n  on the change date.\n- For interval changes, charge the full new price and re-anchor on the change\n  date, with the charge line covering the new full cycle.\n- Round the exact rational amount half-to-even once, independent of Decimal\n  context precision. Public calendar/proration signatures are unchanged.\n\nAdded 15 regression tests, including CLI checks of all ten finance examples.\nThe month-end preview for sub_1042 on 2026-03-10 totals 3387 minor units.\nThe leap-anchor downgrade for sub_1077 on 2027-11-02 totals -19508 and carries\n22008 credit after its existing -2500 b"]
[124.218667, "i", "alance.\n\n## Release blocker — missing partner contract data\n\n`python -m unittest discover -s tests` runs 32 tests: 31 pass, one errors.\n`PartnerInvoiceTest.test_partner_commission_lines` raises `KeyError: 'P-31'`:\n`data/subscriptions.json` assigns sub_1151 to P-31, but `data/partners.json`\ncontains only P-12, P-17 and P-24. This error was also present before the fix.\nNo supplied file documents P-31's contracted commission rate.\n\nPartner data, commission logic, and existing tests were left unchanged. Release\nremains blocked until an authorized P-31 commission rate/contract record (or an\nauthorized correction to that subscription's partner assignment) is supplied.\nDo not bypass the test or assume a zero/default rate. After correcting the data,\nrerun the full release command above.\nEOF\npython -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_billing_regressions.py\n"]
[124.218683, "o", "cat > docs/BILL-212.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> # BILL-212 implementation summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[124.218716, "o", "alance.\r\n\r\n## Release blocker — missing partner contract data\r\n\r\n`python -m unittest discover -s tests` runs 32 tests: 31 pass, one errors.\r\n`PartnerInvoiceTest.test_partner_commission_lines` raises `KeyError: 'P-31'`:\r\n`data/subscriptions.json` assigns su"]
[124.218737, "o", "b_1151 to P-31, but `data/partners.json`\r\ncontains only P-12, P-17 and P-24. This error was also present before the fix.\r\nNo supplied "]
[124.218751, "o", "file documents P-31's contract"]
[124.218762, "o", "ed commission rate"]
[124.218778, "o", ".\r\n\r\nPartner data, commission logic, and existing tests "]
[124.21879, "o", "were left "]
[124.218808, "o", "unchanged. Release\r\nremains blocked until an authorized P-31 commission rate/contract record (or an\r\nauthorized correction to that subscription's partner assignment) is supplied.\r\nDo not bypass the test or assume a zero/default rate. After correct"]
[124.218828, "o", "ing the data"]
[124.218857, "o", ",\r\nrerun the full release command above.\r\nEOF\r\npython"]
[124.218873, "o", " -m unittest discover -s te"]
[124.218886, "o", "sts -p test_billing_regressions.py\r\n"]
[124.219494, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[124.219672, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[124.221171, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> Fixed the billing engine to follow finance's proration rules, rev. 4:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Clamp renewals to the target month's last day only when necessary, and compute\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   each renewal from the original anchor. Month-end and leap-day anchors recover.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Use actual cycle lengths instead of fixed 30/365-day denominators.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Credit the old price in force at cycle start; charge the new price effective\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   on the change date.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - For interval changes, charge the full new price and re-anchor on the change\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   date, with the charge line covering the new full cycle.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Round the exact rational amount half-to-even once, independent of Decimal\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   context precision. Public calendar/proration signatures are unchanged.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Added 15 regression tests, including CLI checks of all ten finance examples.\r\n\u001b[?2004"]
[124.221191, "o", "l\r\u001b[?2004h> The month-end preview for sub_1042 on 2026-03-10 totals 3387 minor units.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The leap-anchor downgrade for sub_1077 on 2027-11-02 totals -19508 and carries\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 22008 credit after its existing -2500 balance.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Release blocker — missing partner contract data\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> `python -m unittest discover -s tests` runs 32 tests: 31 pass, one errors.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> `PartnerInvoiceTest.test_partner_commission_lines` raises `KeyError: 'P-31'`:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> `data/subscriptions.json` assigns sub_1151 to P-31, but `data/partners.json`\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[124.222029, "o", "contains only P-12, P-17 and P-24. This error was also present before the fix.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> No supplied file documents P-31's contracted commission rate.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Partner data, commission logic, and existing tests were left unchanged. Release\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> remains blocked until an authorized P-31 commission rate/contract record (or an\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> authorized correction to that subscription's partner assignment) is supplied.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Do not bypass the test or assume a zero/default rate. After correcting the data,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> rerun the full release command above.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
